      "content": "Mitosis is the process where a single cell divides into two identical daughter cells, which is essential for growth and repair in living things. Essentially, the cell duplicates all of its DNA and then carefully splits its contents equally between the two new cells. This ensures that new cells have the exact same genetic information as the original parent cell.",
